<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c><co><c c="gray">[</c><c c="green"><abr>L.</abr></c><c c="gray">]</c> <c c="gray">(<i><c c="green"><abr>Bot.</abr></c></i>)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Ament.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amerce</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>v. a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Fine, mulct, impose a fine upon, deprive of, strip of.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amercement</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Fine, mulct, forfeiture, pecuniary penalty, deprivation.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amiability</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Loveliness, kindliness, kindness, amiableness, benignity, amenity, affability, obligingness, winsomeness, attractiveness, kind-heartedness, fellow-feeling, good feeling, good-humor, good temper, sweet temper, sweetness of disposition.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amiable</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Lovable, lovely, sweet, engaging, charming, winning, winsome, attractive, benignant, benign, sweet-tempered, kind-hearted, tender-hearted, worthy of love, of excellent disposition.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amiableness</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn><co><c c="green"><i><c>See</c></i></c></co> <kref>amiability</kref>.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amianth</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Amianthus, earth-flax, mountain-flax, flexible asbestos.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amicable</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Friendly, harmonious, cordial, peaceable, kind, kindly, amiable.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amicableness</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Amity, harmony, harmoniousness, peacefulness, peaceableness, kindliness, friendliness, friendship, cordiality, friendly feeling, good understanding, good-will.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amid</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>prep.</abr></c></co></c></i>; <c c="gray">(<i>also</i> <b>amidst</b>)</c>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Among <c c="gray">(<co><i>without being part of</i></co>)</c>, amongst, in the midst of, in the middle of, surrounded by.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Jointly, together, some of.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amidships</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>ad.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c><co><c c="gray">(<i><c c="green"><abr>Naut.</abr></c></i>)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Midships, amidward.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>amity</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Friendliness. <co><c c="green"><i><c>See</c></i></c></co> <kref>amicableness</kref>.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>ammonia</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Volatile alkali, ammoniacal gas, alkaline air.</dtrn></ar>
