<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Similar <c c="gray">(<co><i>in relations</i> or <i>uses</i></co>)</c>, resembling, alike, like, cognate, parallel, corresponding, allied, of a piece.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>analogue</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Correspondent, parallel, counterpart, similar feature <i>or</i> trait, analogon.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>analogy</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Similarity <c c="gray">(<co><i>in relations</i> or <i>uses</i></co>)</c>, resemblance, likeness, parallelism, similitude, parity, correspondence.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>analysis</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Resolution, decomposition, dissection, separation <c c="gray">(<co><i>of elements</i></co>)</c>.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Algebra, calculus, analytics.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <dtrn>Parsing.</dtrn></ar>
