<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Petitioner, solicitor, suitor, candidate.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>application</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Applying, putting on.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Thing applied <c c="gray">(<co>emollient, irritant, stimulant, <i>or</i> rubefacient</co>)</c>.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <dtrn>Appliance, use, exercise, practice.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">4. </c> <dtrn>Solicitation, petition, appeal, request, suit.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">5. </c> <dtrn>Assiduity, industry, perseverance, persistency, intense study, close attention.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">6. </c> <dtrn>Reference to practice, use in detail, putting into practice, turning upon particulars, exemplification.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>apply to</k>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Suit, fit, be adapted to, be suitable to, be applicable to, hold true of, hold of, bear upon, refer to.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Solicit, petition, request, appeal to, call upon, make application to, have recourse to.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>appoint</k>
