 <dtrn>Pupil <c c="gray">(<co><i>in Christianity</i></co>)</c>, neophyte, convert, proselyte.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>categorical</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Positive, absolute, unconditional, unqualified, unreserved, downright, express, explicit, direct, emphatic.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>category</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Class, head, division, order, rank.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Head of predication, predicable, predicament <c c="gray">(<co><i>predicate</i></co>)</c>, leading predicate, universal aspect, supreme distinction, primitive <i>or</i> elemental <i>or</i> elementary relation.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>catenation</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Connection, union, conjunction, linking together, continuous junction, concatenation, intimate connection.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>cater</k>
