 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Sensibility, sensitiveness.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Irritability, irascibility, passionateness, hot temper.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>excitable</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Sensitive, susceptible, impressible.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Irascible, irritable, passionate, choleric, hasty, hot-tempered, quick-tempered.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>excite</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>v. a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Arouse, rouse, awaken, evoke, provoke, call forth, stimulate, incite, animate, kindle, inflame, brew, stir up.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Raise, create, evoke, elicit, give rise to, put in motion.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <dtrn>Disturb, agitate, discompose, irritate, provoke.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>excitement</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Excitation, exciting. See the verb, under 1 and 2.</dtrn>
