 <c><co><c c="gray">[</c><c c="green"><abr>Fr.</abr></c><c c="gray">]</c></co></c> <dtrn>Married women.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>feme-sole</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>; <c c="gray">(<i>also</i> <b>femme-sole</b>)</c>
 <c><co><c c="gray">[</c><c c="green"><abr>Fr.</abr></c><c c="gray">]</c> <c c="gray">(<c c="green"><i>Law</i></c>.)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Single woman, unmarried woman.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>feminality</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Womanhood, femineity, female nature, feminineness, feminacy.</dtrn></ar>
