<ar><k>objective</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Belonging to <i>or</i> characterizing the object <c c="gray">(<co><i>as distinguished from the subject</i></co>)</c>.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Outward, external, real, actual, positive, true, unconditional, universal, non-subjective, free from subjective limits.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <dtrn>Absorbed in objects, non-introversive, free from introversion, wholly occupied with the object <i>or</i> fact, that tells things as they are, that does not color facts, that paints things in their own light, extroitive <c c="gray">(<i><co>rare</co></i>)</c>.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">4. </c> <c><co><c c="gray">(<i><c c="green"><abr>Gram.</abr></c></i>)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Denoting the object <i>or</i> regimen <i>or</i> complement.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">5. </c> <c><co><c c="gray">(<i><c c="green"><abr>Mil.</abr></c></i>)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Destined, aimed at, of chief aim, of ultimate strategy.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>objectless</k>
<i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Aimless, purposeless, wandering, vague, desultory.</dtrn></ar>
