 <c c="blue">5. </c> <dtrn>Publish, issue, make public.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">6. </c> <dtrn>Dislocate, luxate.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">7. </c> <dtrn>Confuse, disconcert, interrupt.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">8. </c> <dtrn>Offend, displease, anger, provoke, vex, irritate.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">9. </c> <dtrn>Place at interest.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>put out of countenance</k>
 <dtrn>Shame, mortify, abash.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>put over</k>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Place in command of, give authority over.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Defer, postpone, put off.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <dtrn>Refer, send.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">4. </c> <dtrn>Sail over.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>putrescence</k>
