<c c="blue">II</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>v. a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Supply with pasturage, graze, turn out to pasture.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>pat</k>
<c c="blue">I</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c><co><c c="gray">(<i><c c="green"><abr>Colloq.</abr></c></i>)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Fit, apt, pertinent, suitable, appropriate.</dtrn>
<c c="blue">II</c>. <c c="green"><abr><co><c><i>ad.</i></c></co></abr></c>
 <c><co><c c="gray">(<c c="green"><abr><c c="green"><i>Colloq.</i></c></abr></c>)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Seasonably, fitly, aptly, conveniently, <i>apropos.</i></dtrn>
<c c="blue">III</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Rap, dab, tap, hit, light blow.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Small lump, cake.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <co><c><c c="gray">(<c c="green"><abr><c c="green"><i>Colloq.</i></c></abr></c>)</c> [Abbreviated from <i>St. Patrick</i>, their patron saint.<c c="gray">]</c></c></co> <dtrn>Irishman, paddy, Milesian, Hibernian, son of Erin.</dtrn>
<c c="blue">IV</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>v. a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Rap, dab, tap, strike lightly, hit.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>patient</k>
<c c="blue">I</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Enduring, able to endure.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Submissive, resigned, uncomplaining, unrepining, passive, long-suffering.</dtrn>
