<c c="blue">II</c>. <c c="green"><abr><co><c><i>n.</i></c></co></abr></c>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Falling back, return to a former state <c c="gray">(<co><i>especially a bad state</i></co>)</c>, lapse, backsliding.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Falling back, return to a former state.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>relative</k>
<c c="blue">I</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Referring <c c="gray">(<co><i>to something else</i></co>)</c>, not absolute.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Respecting, relating to, pertaining to, belonging to, connected with.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <dtrn>Particular, special, positive, definite, pertinent, relevant.</dtrn>
<c c="blue">II</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Relation, kinsman, connection.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <c><co><c c="gray">(<i><c c="green"><abr>Gram.</abr></c></i>)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Relative pronoun.</dtrn></ar>
