<ar><k>seam</k>
<c c="blue">I</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>n.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Suture, commissure, joint, line of juncture.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Fissure, crevice.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <c><co><c c="gray">(<c c="green"><i>Mining</i></c>.)</c></co></c> <dtrn>Thin layer, stratum, <i>or</i> bed; narrow vein.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">4. </c> <dtrn>Scar, cicatrice, cicatrix.</dtrn>
<c c="blue">II</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>v. a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Unite, join together.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Scar, mark with a cicatrix, line.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>sear</k>
<c c="blue">I</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>v. a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Dry, wither.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">2. </c> <dtrn>Cauterize, burn with a hot iron, burn with cautery, scorch.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">3. </c> <dtrn>Make callous, make insensible.</dtrn>
 <c c="blue">4. </c> <dtrn>Brand.</dtrn>
<c c="blue">II</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <dtrn>Dry, withered, sere.</dtrn></ar>
<ar><k>search</k>
<c c="blue">I</c>. <i><c><co><c c="darkorange"><abr>v. a.</abr></c></co></c></i>
 <c c="blue">1. </c> <dtrn>Examine, explore, scrutinize, investigate, overhaul, sift, inspect, look into, search into, pry into, peer into.</dtrn>
